## 1. Solid Queue recurring jobs

**`config/recurring.yml`** — the scheduler config Solid Queue reads at boot.

```yaml
production:
  # Clear finished jobs every hour so the tables don't grow unbounded
  clear_solid_queue_finished_jobs:
    command: "SolidQueue::Job.clear_finished_in_batches(sleep_between_batches: 0.3)"
    schedule: every hour at minute 12

  # Nightly cleanup of old Active Storage blobs (if you use it)
  purge_orphaned_attachments:
    command: "AttachmentPurgeJob.perform_later"
    schedule: every day at 3am

  # Example: send a daily digest email
  daily_digest:
    command: "DailyDigestJob.perform_later"
    schedule: every day at 6am

staging:
  clear_solid_queue_finished_jobs:
    command: "SolidQueue::Job.clear_finished_in_batches(sleep_between_batches: 0.3)"
    schedule: every hour at minute 12

development:
  # nothing scheduled in dev
```

**`config/queue.yml`** — worker pools and their concurrency.

```yaml
default: &default
  dispatchers:
    - polling_interval: 1
      batch_size: 500
      concurrency_maintenance_interval: 300
  workers:
    - queues: "*"
      threads: 3
      processes: <%= ENV.fetch("JOB_CONCURRENCY", 1) %>
      polling_interval: 0.1

development:
  <<: *default

test:
  <<: *default

production:
  <<: *default
```

**`config/environments/production.rb`** — enable the Solid Queue plugin if running Puma with the embedded job process:

```ruby
config.solid_queue.connects_to = { database: { writing: :queue } }
# or, if running jobs in Puma:
# plugin :solid_queue
```

**`Gemfile`**
```ruby
gem "solid_queue"
gem "mission_control-jobs"   # optional web UI at /jobs
```

Then in `config/routes.rb`:
```ruby
mount MissionControl::Jobs::Engine, at: "/jobs" if defined?(MissionControl::Jobs)
```

Kamal already runs the job process via `servers.job.cmd: bin/jobs` from the deploy config — nothing else to change.

